From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tsuji Riya <tsuji.riya@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 03:14:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 28/28] ARM: configs: Add cnc1800l_defconfig

Add a defconfig for the D-Link DSM-232: zImage with the DTB appended
(ARM_APPENDED_DTB and ATAG_DTB_COMPAT, as the vendor U-Boot cannot
pass a DTB), the drivers of the board, USB storage with ext4 and vfat,
the AR6003 Wi-Fi, the HDMI console and kexec.

VFP is enabled for armhf userlands such as Alpine. Wi-Fi power save is
off by default: with it, ping times on hardware varied between 27 and
322ms, without it they stay around 20ms (the vendor also turned it
off). kexec lets a test kernel be started from a running system, so a
kernel that does not come up is left by a power cycle.

Signed-off-by: Tsuji Riya <tsuji.riya@gmail.com>
---
 MAINTAINERS                         |  2 +
 arch/arm/configs/cnc1800l_defconfig | 90 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 92 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 arch/arm/configs/cnc1800l_defconfig

